Ely: patch logs reach the app in release builds

The engines build without --enable-sal-log, so SAL_INFO and SAL_WARN
compile to nothing: every log line the earlier Ely patches added was
never written. include/ely/log.hxx adds ELY_INFO, ELY_WARN and
ELY_WARN_IF. They are always compiled, take the area "ely." plus the
given one, skip the SAL_LOG selector and go through sal_detail_log,
which writes to stderr unless SAL_LOG_FILE (or logging.ini on Windows)
names a file; the Ely worker passes those lines on to the app's log. Every
patch log moves to them. The pivot, chart and linked-object messages
drop their arguments, which can hold text from the document. Only the
twelve files that include the new header rebuild.

